# The scratch image builds the binary INSIDE itself (docker/scratch.Dockerfile), so the build context
# is the source tree — and these are the parts of it that must not travel.
#
# `.git` is excluded, which has a visible consequence rather than none: `KoreBuildIdentity` stamps
# `commit = unknown` in that image. It already does on the Linux box, whose mutagen replica carries
# no `.git` either. The alternative is worse than it looks — a file git TRACKS but `.dockerignore`
# excludes reads as deleted inside the build, and the stamp becomes `-dirty` for ever.
.git
.github
build
*/build
.gradle
.kotlin
.idea
docs
